 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic; the joke is on each disguise, never on a person. Nobody is hurt in any case; no weapon and no force are shown (the Louisa case was a shoplifting, not a robbery, and is never called one). The two Louisa men (one arrested and charged in May 2020, accused only, no outcome found; the other never identified in the reports), the two men arrested in Spain in 2011 and the Brooklyn man convicted in 2012 are never named on screen or in narration and are drawn ONLY as dark rim-lit silhouettes tagged NOT A LIKENESS (the watermelon heads and the wig-and-sunglasses disguise are drawn over featureless silhouettes). Allegations are attributed ('police say', ACCUSED / CHARGED labels, AS OF OCT 2026); the conviction and sentence are stated only for the Brooklyn case. The clerk, officers, driver, investigator and passer-by are generic figures. The store is a generic shop (no chain name, sign or trade dress); the coach has no livery; the posted 'security image' and the tombstone photo are our own plain typed graphics, not real footage or documents. Facts verified 2026-10-19.",
