 "claims": [
  {
   "id": "K_hook",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "5/6 May 2020 (the reports differ on the date), about 9:30 pm, Louisa, Virginia: police said two men wearing hollowed-out watermelons with eye holes cut out walked into a convenience store and committed a larceny (shoplifting), arriving in a lifted 2006 black Toyota Tacoma. Narration: 'Police say two thieves wore watermelon heads.' Headline 'POLICE SAY TWO THIEVES / WORE WATERMELON HEADS'. The store chain is not named on screen.",
   "sources": [
    "wric",
    "cbsbalt",
    "lawcrime",
    "sixabc",
    "fox5dc"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_took",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Police said the pair took alcohol from the store. Narration: 'Then they took alcohol.'",
   "sources": [
    "wric",
    "lawcrime",
    "cbsbalt",
    "globalnews"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_posted",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The Louisa Police Department posted the security images on Facebook and asked for the public's help identifying the two; commenters said they had seen the pair elsewhere in town; about ten days later (announced 15-16 May 2020) police said one arrest had been made and thanked the community. Narration: 'Police posted the pictures, then made an arrest.'",
   "sources": [
    "lawcrime",
    "wric",
    "wvir",
    "cbsbalt",
    "globalnews"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_charged",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The arrested man, 20, was charged with wearing a mask in public while committing larceny, petit larceny of alcohol and underage possession of alcohol; police were still seeking the second man. ACCUSED only: no plea, conviction or sentence was found in any extract (AS OF OCT 2026). Label 'ONE MAN, 20, CHARGED'.",
   "sources": [
    "wric",
    "cbsbalt",
    "lawcrime",
    "nbcwash",
    "ctv"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_felony",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "FUN FACT: in Virginia, wearing a mask or other device to conceal your identity in a public place (over the age of 16, outside the statutory exceptions) is a Class 6 felony under Code of Virginia s. 18.2-422; the law was suspended during the 2020-21 COVID emergency order and is tied by legal commentators to 1950s anti-Klan legislation.",
   "sources": [
    "vacode",
    "valawyer",
    "vadogwood"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_suitcase",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "June 2011, Spain: police said a thief rode inside a suitcase in the luggage hold of the airport coach between Girona and Barcelona, climbed out during the ride and stole from other passengers' bags (a laptop and a GPS unit were reported); an accomplice bought the ticket, loaded the case and collected it. Narration: 'Spain: a thief rode in a suitcase.'",
   "sources": [
    "cbsnews",
    "foxnews",
    "abc7",
    "time"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_minutes",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "COUNTER: the Girona-Barcelona coach ride is roughly 90 minutes (about 100 km). Counter '90' with the label 'MINUTES IN THE LUGGAGE HOLD'.",
   "sources": [
    "cbsnews",
    "foxnews"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_warm",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "On 3 June 2011 a driver noticed a passenger struggling with a very heavy suitcase and called police; officers knocked on the case, found it unusually warm and opened it on a sweating man. Narration: 'Police knocked: the case was warm.'",
   "sources": [
    "cbsnews",
    "foxnews",
    "abc7",
    "time"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_arrested",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The man in the suitcase and his accomplice on board, both Polish nationals, were arrested on theft charges. Narration: 'Inside, a sweating man. Both arrested.' Neither is named in the reports; the accomplice is a silhouette tagged NOT A LIKENESS.",
   "sources": [
    "cbsnews",
    "foxnews",
    "time"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_mother",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Brooklyn, New York: after his mother died in 2003 (aged 73), a Park Slope man impersonated her for about six years in a blond wig, dress and oversized sunglasses. Narration: 'The strangest lasted six years.' / 'A Brooklyn man dressed as his dead mother.'",
   "sources": [
    "ap_ktar",
    "ap_sowetan",
    "nbcny",
    "bkpaper",
    "reuters_ttw"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_cheques",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Prosecutors said he cashed her Social Security cheques (reported as about $44,000 or $52,000; no figure is shown) and used the impersonation to hold on to her $2.2 million brownstone, even renewing her driver's licence in person. Label 'SOCIAL SECURITY CHEQUES · A $2.2M BROWNSTONE'.",
   "sources": [
    "ap_ktar",
    "ap_sowetan",
    "reuters_ttw",
    "elderlaw"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_gotcha",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "When investigators from the Brooklyn district attorney's office met 'her', he arrived in a red cardigan, lipstick and manicured nails, breathing through an oxygen tank; the investigators already had a photo of her tombstone. Narration: 'Investigators met \"her\" with her grave photo.'",
   "sources": [
    "ap_ktar",
    "ap_sowetan",
    "iol",
    "reuters_ttw",
    "elderlaw"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_sentence",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Convicted by a jury on 3 May 2012 of grand larceny, mortgage fraud and forgery among other counts; sentenced on 21 May 2012 to 13 2/3 to 41 years in prison. Narration: 'Convicted: up to forty-one years.' Label 'SENTENCED: 13 2/3 TO 41 YEARS'.",
   "sources": [
    "ap_ktar",
    "ap_sowetan",
    "iol",
    "elderlaw",
    "reuters_ttw"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_underage",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "CALLBACK: the haul was alcohol and the arrested man was 20: among his charges, underage possession of alcohol (accused only). Narration: 'The haul? Alcohol, and he was twenty.' (the end label adds 'underage possession of alcohol')",
   "sources": [
    "wric",
    "cbsbalt",
    "lawcrime",
    "nbcwash"
   ]
  }
 ],
